            <ArticleTitle>A case of chest pain and hemoptysis in a young child.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>152-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/LBR.0000000000000130</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Endobronchial atypical carcinoid tumors are rare in young children and can have a varied presentation. Early diagnosis and surgical resection provide an excellent outcome and good long-term survival. However, due to the risk of recurrence and later metastasis, long-term follow-up is necessary.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
